From 5ad0bdcf60b3409383fb00fbb37e90c040a69786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:31:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: FakeHub lease release always emits the
 run-outcome event and honors outcome

Follow-up to PR #1896 review 5886812281 (non-blocking nit). The fake's
leases release wrote a `released` event only for unused_grant and ignored
`outcome`. As hermes-hub transitions.ts releaseTask, it now always appends
the run-outcome event carrying retry_status (review when the run was
claimed out of review), maps neutral outcomes through NEUTRAL_RELEASES
(run outcome + event kind, owner_restart metadata), ends terminal_provider
as crashed with the canonical notice, and sets unused_grant only for a
plain released outcome. The card goes back to its retry lane only while
running. Failure accounting stays on FakeService.release_op (ops path).

Test-only change.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_fake_board.py    | 69 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_rejections.py | 34 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

